2745..2820 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every word: the round trip at a variable, by"
2821..2895 Comment "/// induction over the presented words. The result type reads the word the"
2896..2967 Comment "/// fold descends on, so each arm answers it at its constructor and the"
2968..3026 Comment "/// recursive call at the field: `sectWords[<](x)` relates"
3027..3102 Comment "/// `spinWords(windWords(x))` to `x`, and carried along `around` it relates"
3103..3177 Comment "/// `Loop(spinWords(windWords(x)))`, which `spinWords(windWords(Loop(x)))`"
3178..3255 Comment "/// runs to, to `Loop(x)`. The case respects both rules: at `Loop(Unloop(x))`"
3256..3330 Comment "/// the arms compose to `cong(around, cong(unaround, p))`, whose functions"
3331..3407 Comment "/// compose to the identity under the rules, so the chain is `p` itself, the"
3408..3426 Comment "/// answer at `x`."
